Third-party components:

This project's own code (boot/, smp/, stubs/, test_harness.c, Makefile,
scripts/) is MIT-licensed as above. It is designed to build against
FFmpeg (http://ffmpeg.org), which this repository does not redistribute;
FFmpeg is fetched from upstream by scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.sh.

FFmpeg is licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License version 2.1
or later (LGPL-2.1-or-later). The configure line in scripts/fetch-ffmpeg.sh
does NOT enable --enable-gpl or --enable-nonfree, so libraries built by it
are LGPL. The full license text ships with this repository as
COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and with the FFmpeg source tree.

If you build binaries with this project you must comply with LGPL section 6:
provide recipients a way to relink or rebuild your application with a
modified FFmpeg. Because this repository ships the complete build recipe
(source fetch, configure flags, Makefile) and links only unmodified upstream
static archives, rebuilding from this repository satisfies that requirement.
Consider using --enable-shared for stricter compliance if you distribute
binaries directly.

External libraries used at runtime inside the guest: none beyond FFmpeg and
libgcc. Host-side builds may link zlib/bzip2 (zlib and bzip2 licenses).
